  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Son nica is the Nicaraguan popular song genre created by the composer Camilo Zapata, regarded as its father, and developed by composers such as Víctor M. Leiva, drawing on the rural sones and marimba dances of the Pacific region in a lilting triple metre. Its songs portray country life, local places and national pride and are sung with guitars and marimba; Carlos Mejía Godoy's recordings later carried its rhythms into Nicaraguan national song.",
